@page "/terms"

<PageTitle>Terms - Clarity Belongs</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="Clarity Belongs public V1 terms for accounts, monitoring, alerts, availability, and paid membership." />
</HeadContent>

<div class="shell public-shell article-shell">
    <header class="hero compact-hero article-hero">
        <div class="eyebrow">TERMS</div>
        <h1>Use Clarity as an awareness tool.</h1>
        <p class="public-lead">Clarity helps observe public sources and preserve history. It does not guarantee that every change will be detected or delivered immediately.</p>
    </header>

    <article class="article-body legal-copy">
        <section>
            <h2>Service scope</h2>
            <p>Clarity Belongs provides self-service monitoring, observation history, comparison, and notification tools. Availability, source behavior, network conditions, third-party data, and external providers can affect results.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h2>Your responsibility</h2>
            <p>You are responsible for choosing targets you are permitted to monitor and for deciding how to act on the information Clarity provides. Do not use the service to probe private systems, evade access controls, or submit secrets.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h2>No guaranteed detection</h2>
            <p>Clarity is designed to reduce repeated manual checking, not to provide a guarantee that every event, outage, change, expiration, or notification will be detected or delivered within a specific time.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h2>Membership and billing</h2>
            <p>Plan limits control active follows, minimum check cadence, and external delivery features. Paid subscriptions are handled through Stripe-hosted checkout and billing management. Final public prices, refund terms, and cancellation wording will be published before the paid release gate is opened.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h2>Changes and availability</h2>
            <p>The service is still being built and tested. Features, limits, adapters, and provider integrations may change as reliability and operating cost are measured.</p>
        </section>
        <p class="legal-note">Draft public-V1 terms. Final legal review, effective date, business/contact details, refund language, and jurisdiction provisions remain part of the release checklist.</p>
    </article>
</div>
